1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,344
Chapter thirteen — ship it.

2
00:00:03,404 --> 00:00:15,316
A design that cannot leave
the tool is a drawing.

3
00:00:15,376 --> 00:00:24,821
Deploy opens on the plan: every service,
where it runs, and what it costs.

4
00:00:24,881 --> 00:00:34,326
Thirteen services, the target domains,
projected monthly cost and storage.

5
00:00:34,386 --> 00:00:49,195
That total is the same number the
canvas has been showing all along.

6
00:00:49,255 --> 00:01:05,460
Then pick an artifact. Docker Compose
for a laptop or a single host.

7
00:01:05,520 --> 00:01:19,386
Kubernetes manifests for a cluster.

8
00:01:19,446 --> 00:01:35,766
Azure Bicep for the managed services
— Cosmos, Blob, and the rest.

9
00:01:35,826 --> 00:01:49,256
Terraform if that is your house style.

10
00:01:49,316 --> 00:02:00,343
And Ansible for the machines you already own.

11
00:02:00,403 --> 00:02:12,716
It is a scaffold, honestly labelled — set your
secrets, images and networking before you apply it.

12
00:02:12,776 --> 00:02:16,718
The design went in as a sentence.

13
00:02:16,778 --> 00:02:20,980
It comes out as something you can run.
